{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission.json\", \"summary\": \"Submitted a feedback-only research closeout product recording an investigated and explained anomaly, with preflight returning valid:true. The anomaly: after the receiver installed a snapshot at index 43 in the commit-context prefix, the node reported its last index as 43 while Stats reported last_log_index as 1, which looked like an inconsistent publication. The explanation is that the two exports name different quantities and both are accurate: Raft.LastIndex() returns the last index in stable storage, taking the greater of the cached last log and the last snapshot (documented as such), so it is 43, while Stats publishes last_log_index and last_log_term from the cached last log entry alone, which in this prefix is the bootstrap configuration entry at index 1, with the same Stats map reporting last_snapshot_index 43 beside it; the harness's injection removed no entries since TrailingLogs is large and compactLogs did nothing, so the log store genuinely ends at index 1. No obligation, check, map change or evidence is claimed for it, because the sources answer the specific suspicion rather than leaving a defect premise. Remaining items are restated: whether the two names warrant a documentation change is presentation not obligation; the mechanism returning a campaigning non-voter to follower is still unidentified (nothing in the grant path tests a candidate's suffrage, and both exploration prefixes ended with the target as a follower, never leading); the transfer path still accepts a non-voter target and reports success with no leader established, uncovered by any obligation; the repair locations for the three newest obligations and the deferred third-party-transport and nested-module surfaces remain open; and none of the exploration or construction runs are offered as property evidence. Run state at this point: ten confirmed in-scope findings across eight units, audit spec v13 with all units checked, 2 audit units, 21 experiments and about seven minutes remaining.\"}"}}
